      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "FARRAIGE (1) has the most persuasive recent profile, coming off a Benchmark 58 second at Kempsey where he was beaten just over half a length after looming to win, and his earlier fourth in a 3yo+ Benchmark 66 at Taree reads well for this grade. The rise to 2200m is the obvious test, but his current form is the right starting point. DIPIERDOMENICO (3) is the main danger, backing up quickly after making ground in a Benchmark 58 at Tamworth and bringing a genuine distance record into the race. RITA'S PEARL (6) has not won this season, yet the return to a suitable trip and her Kempsey fourth keep her in the minor-money mix. CALEDONIAN (2) has the right Benchmark 66 grounding, was not fully suited when wide and tightened last start, and his Taree third gives him a live each-way platform if he handles the weight.",
